  "description": "Teaser and the Firecat is the fifth studio album by Cat Stevens, released in October 1971. It was recorded between July 1970 and March 1971, and features 10 songs, including the hits \"Morning Has Broken\", \"Moonshadow\" and \"Peace Train\". The album was a commercial success, surpassing the heights achieved by Stevens' previous album, Tea for the Tillerman, reaching both the UK and US top 3 and also spending fifteen weeks at the top of the Australian charts, becoming the biggest-selling album of the country in 1972 and winning Biggest Selling LP at the 1972 King of Pop Awards. It also shares a title with a children's book written and illustrated by Stevens, which focuses on the characters from the album cover.",
